📢 Circular No. 259/05/2026-GST dated 26 October 2026
CBIC Clarifies on Issues related to Pre-Deposit Requirements under Section 107(6) and 112(8) of the CGST Act, 2017
Key Highlights:
▪️ Admitted Amount vs. Disputed Tax: The admitted liability must be paid in full, while the prescribed 10% pre-deposit is calculated on the disputed tax amount.
▪️ Appeal before GSTAT: The 10% pre-deposit is calculated on the disputed tax liability confirmed by the Appellate Authority, in addition to the amount deposited at the first appellate stage.
▪️ Refund of Pre-Deposit: Refund may be claimed through FORM GST RFD-01 under “On account of order”. A favourable order need not expressly direct the refund.
▪️ Departmental Appeal: Refund cannot be denied merely because the Department intends to file, or has filed, a further appeal, unless the favourable order is stayed by the Appellate Tribunal or Court.
▪️ Interest on Refund: Interest computation is based on the actual date of payment of pre-deposit determined separately at each appellate stage.
▪️ Remand Cases: In partial remand cases, the amount corresponding to the demand confirmed in favour of the Revenue, along with applicable interest, must be recovered or adjusted before refunding the balance.
📌 The Circular promotes uniformity and clarity regarding GST appeal pre-deposits and their refunds.
